From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Lebedev <sergey@lebedev.mobi>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:26:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mips: econet: add multi-vpe capability to EN751221

Backport of upstream commit 8ae6e79ee0ce ("mips: econet: add multi-vpe
capability to EN751221"), which landed in v7.3.

EN751221 has no Coherence Manager, so register_cps_smp_ops() always fails
on this SoC and device_tree_init() fell straight through to
register_up_smp_ops() -- one CPU, even though the 34Kc core implements the
MT ASE with two VPEs per MVPConf0.PVPE. Registering vsmp_smp_ops brings the
second VPE up under SMVP, one TC per VPE.

vsmp_smp_ops' generic init_secondary() unmasks IP0/IP1 plus either a GIC or
Malta's cascading IP6/IP7 performance-counter lines. econet's INTC is
neither, and unmasking anything past IP0/IP1/IP2 stops it delivering
interrupts at all, so init_secondary is overridden to unmask only the two
software-interrupt lines the generic IPI layer needs. Device IRQs do not go
through Status.IM here: the INTC driver dispatches them per-vector via
set_vi_handler().

Adapted against this tree's EN7528 CPS probe in device_tree_init(), which
upstream's base does not carry -- the CPS attempt stays first and the SMVP
registration is tried only when it fails. The Kconfig hunk likewise only
adds SYS_SUPPORTS_MULTITHREADING instead of replacing SMP/SMP_UP/
SYS_SUPPORTS_SMP, since EN7528 still needs those here.

Signed-off-by: Sergey Lebedev <sergey@lebedev.mobi>
---
--- a/arch/mips/econet/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/econet/Kconfig
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ choice
 		select PCI_DRIVERS_GENERIC
 		select SMP
 		select SMP_UP
+		select SYS_SUPPORTS_MULTITHREADING
 		select SYS_SUPPORTS_SMP
 		help
 		  The EN751221 family includes EN7512, RN7513, EN7521, EN7526.
--- a/arch/mips/econet/init.c
+++ b/arch/mips/econet/init.c
@@ -33,6 +33,41 @@ static void hw_reset(char *command)
 	iowrite32(RESET, CR_AHB_RSTCR);
 }
 
+/*
+ * vsmp_init_secondary expects either GIC or cascading interrupt configuration.
+ * The EN751221 is a 34Kc with VEIC, but not GIC compatible. The cascading
+ * configuration enables lines 6 and 7 for performance counters, but when this
+ * is done on the EN751221 intc with VEIC enabled, it causes the whole intc to
+ * stop sending interrupts.
+ * Only unmask lines 0 and 1 (software interrupts) in init_secondary.
+ */
+#ifdef CONFIG_MIPS_MT_SMP
+extern const struct plat_smp_ops vsmp_smp_ops;
+static struct plat_smp_ops en75_smp_ops __ro_after_init;
+
+static void en751221_init_secondary(void)
+{
+	write_c0_status((read_c0_status() & ~ST0_IM) |
+		(STATUSF_IP0 | STATUSF_IP1));
+}
+
+static int __init en751221_register_vsmp_smp_ops(void)
+{
+	if (!cpu_has_mipsmt)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	en75_smp_ops = vsmp_smp_ops;
+	en75_smp_ops.init_secondary = en751221_init_secondary;
+	register_smp_ops(&en75_smp_ops);
+	return 0;
+}
+#else
+static int __init en751221_register_vsmp_smp_ops(void)
+{
+	return -ENODEV;
+}
+#endif /* CONFIG_MIPS_MT_SMP */
+
 /* 1. Bring up early printk. */
 void __init prom_init(void)
 {
@@ -68,6 +103,11 @@ void __init device_tree_init(void)
 	if (!register_cps_smp_ops())
 		return;
 
+	/* EN751221 dual-vpe */
+	if (!en751221_register_vsmp_smp_ops())
+		return;
+
+	/* EN751221 with MT_SMP disabled */
 	register_up_smp_ops();
 }
 
